  "billing_semantics": {
    "input_token_semantics": "Anthropic reports input_tokens CACHE-EXCLUSIVE. input_tokens, cache_creation_input_tokens and cache_read_input_tokens are three DISJOINT buckets. On these runs input_tokens reads 2 on every run because essentially the whole prompt is either a cache write or a cache read.",
    "effective_prompt_tokens": "input_tokens + cache_creation_input_tokens + cache_read_input_tokens. Kept as a DESCRIPTIVE metric only. It is never multiplied by a single rate; each bucket is charged at its own rate.",
    "cache_semantics_short": "1-hour writes at $10/MTok, reads at $0.50/MTok, directly observed",
    "cache_semantics": "RESOLVED FROM THE RAW USAGE, NOT INFERRED. usage.cache_creation splits the write into ephemeral_1h_input_tokens and ephemeral_5m_input_tokens. Across all 15 runs every cache-creation token is ephemeral_1h and ephemeral_5m is zero, so the 1-hour write rate ($10/MTok, 2x base input) is the applicable one and the 5-minute rate ($6.25/MTok) never applies. Four runs create the cache (monday-001/002/003/005 run 1) and the rest read it.",
    "reasoning_treatment_short": "already inside billable output_tokens - NOT charged separately",
    "reasoning_treatment": "thinking_tokens is observable in usage.output_tokens_details and is a SUBSET of output_tokens, not an additional bucket. PROVEN TWO WAYS. (1) The pricing page defines no reasoning or thinking token category anywhere; the only output category is 'Output tokens'. (2) The meter settles it directly: charging output_tokens alone reproduces the provider-reported Opus cost to 0.000000000% on all 15 runs, whereas adding thinking_tokens on top would overstate monday-004 run 1 by 69.71% ($1.0258 against a reported $0.6044). Doing output_tokens + thinking_tokens would therefore be double counting, and reasoning_additional_cost is 0 by demonstration rather than by assumption.",
    "output_includes": "answer tokens plus thinking tokens, billed once at the output rate."
  },
  "auxiliary_call_handling": {
    "problem": "The generation route made an auxiliary claude-haiku-4-5 call per run that DISABLE_NON_ESSENTIAL_MODEL_CALLS=1 did not suppress. The route's total_cost_usd therefore covers Claude Code's own overhead as well as the Opus generation.",
    "resolution": "The normalized cost is computed from the claude-opus-5 modelUsage line and its token buckets ONLY. The Haiku line is excluded entirely from the normalized figure and from the reconciliation, and is reported separately so the exclusion is visible rather than silent.",
    "buckets_reported_separately": [
      "route_total_cost_usd",
      "opus_reported_cost_usd",
      "auxiliary_cost_usd"
    ],
    "comparable_figure": "opus_reported_cost_usd is the only route figure that may be compared with the normalized list-price cost. We are pricing the cost of the Opus generation, not the cost of running Claude Code."
  },
